From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: InspurSDN <sdn@ieisystem.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bgpd: Cancel BFD hold timer on peer reset

In bgp_peer_bfd_reset(), the BFD configuration (including hold_time) is
reset to the strict defaults, but the per-peer hold timer (t_hold_timer)
is not cancelled. A stale timer can still fire after the reset and
interfere with the newly configured BFD session, causing spurious BFD
state changes or delayed peer convergence.

Cancel the hold timer together with the rest of the BFD configuration
reset so that a fresh session starts cleanly.

Signed-off-by: InspurSDN <sdn@ieisystem.com>
---
 bgpd/bgp_bfd.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/bgpd/bgp_bfd.c b/bgpd/bgp_bfd.c
index 0d028f133f..46018fce22 100644
--- a/bgpd/bgp_bfd.c
+++ b/bgpd/bgp_bfd.c
@@ -394,6 +394,7 @@ static void bgp_peer_bfd_reset(struct peer *p)
 	p->bfd_config->hold_time = BFD_DEF_STRICT_HOLD_TIME;
 	p->bfd_config->cbit = false;
 	p->bfd_config->profile[0] = 0;
+	event_cancel(&p->bfd_config->t_hold_timer);
 }
 
 void bgp_peer_configure_bfd(struct peer *p, bool manual)
